              heading: 'Part 8',
              text: '“Back to your time!” he warned. Tara stopped playing — and poof! Back in class, she blinked. Her tabla whispered, “Next stop — Maratha Empire?”. GENRE : GENRE: KRITI ch-2_theater.indd ch-2_theater.indd 19-06-2025 15:27:17 19-06-2025 15:27:17 Now that you have peeked into the magical wardrobe of genres — from mysterious boxes to musical ghungroos , it is time for you to start writing. Pick your favourite genre or combine a couple of them. Go ahead and try them all! Who knows? Today, you may be writing a tearjerking tragedy, and tomorrow, a comedy that makes even your dog laugh! You may even create a new genre! The options are limitless. CIRCLE TIME 1. Which is your favourite genre and why? 2. Do you prefer lengthy writing like a novel or a play with acts, or short stories and plays? 3. Read a scene of a script from ancient times and a scene from a contemporary play. Discuss and note do wn the differences in style and thought. Which one do you like more? So grab your pen and paper — your next superhit story awaits. Get your parents and teachers to sit back, and enjoy your show! REMEMBER Do not miss the basics of a story and script that you learnt in Grades and 7. Plan your ‘Beginning — Middle — End’ and find an interesting conflict. This is a must for whatever genre or type of script you write. Children performing a Fantasy Musical',
